According to a report by IntelMarketResearch, the global Clinical Oncology Next Generation Sequencing (NGS) Market was valued at USD 862 million in 2025 and is projected to reach USD 2.136 billion by 2034, expanding at a CAGR of 10.6% during the forecast period. Clinical Oncology NGS refers to high-throughput genetic sequencing technologies used to detect mutations, insertions, deletions, copy-number alterations and chromosomal translocations across solid tumors and hematologic malignancies. By delivering comprehensive molecular profiles from tumor tissue or circulating cell-free DNA, NGS enables oncologists to support targeted-treatment selection, clinical-trial enrollment and treatment-response monitoring.
