Why This Market Matters
Clinical Oncology NGS is becoming an important component of precision cancer care because it can evaluate multiple genetic alterations through a single comprehensive testing workflow. This supports treatment selection, biomarker discovery, clinical-trial matching and longitudinal monitoring.
The market is also benefiting from improvements in liquid biopsy, AI-assisted interpretation and cloud-based bioinformatics. As sequencing costs decline and reimbursement pathways expand, NGS testing is expected to reach a broader range of clinical settings.
